<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Friday it had allocated 4.07 billion guilders to the money market under a seven-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.90 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks received 28.8 percent of the amount they had applied for.</p>
<p>The new liquidity pact replaces a seven-day facility of 3.90 billion guilders which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
